No need, my IT already do this by running the MimeCast email filter [1]. Links to non-whitelist sites are expressed in the format:<p><pre><code>    https:&#x2F;&#x2F;url.uk.m.mimecastprotect.com&#x2F;s&#x2F;&lt;random_string&gt;?domain=&lt;domain_name&gt;
</code></pre>
Maybe I can tell the link is from Google, but not what is likely to be in the URL. It&#x27;s a complete surprise as to whether I will be looking at a web page or downloading something.<p>[1] <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.mimecast.com&#x2F;" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.mimecast.com&#x2F;</a>
